From: aiden build <build@aiden.local>
Subject: [PATCH] adb: C++17 compatibility for string_view starts_with/ends_with

std::string_view::starts_with() and ends_with() are C++20 methods. GCC 8.3
libstdc++ only supports C++17, causing build failures:

  adb_client.cpp:169:18: error: 'using string_view = class
  std::basic_string_view<char>' has no member named 'starts_with'

This patch creates adb_string_view_compat.h with C++17 free-function
equivalents (adb_compat::starts_with/ends_with) and rewrites all call
sites across 7 source files. String-view literal forms like
"foo"sv.starts_with(x) become adb_compat::starts_with("foo"sv, x).

Aiden-local patch (not from upstream nmeum/android-tools).
